[Music]  [Music]  after a weekend of hype at the tokyo  game show we  once again return to the hero's path a  series in which we visualize the  different journeys of some of the most  prominent characters from breath of the  wild  during the great calamity as expected  the team at cuy tecmo didn't spoil too  much in terms of story  showing only gameplay sections taking  place pre-calamity  and even the trailer kept things quite  abstract we did however get to see empi  in action  and were presented with a bit more of an  idea about her role in the story  which is perfect for this episode in  today's topic we will cover the three  most prominent members of the chica  tribe  that being impa herself her sister and  sheikah scientist pura  and ancient technology expert robbie all  of which are still alive during the  events of breath of the wild albeit  older or in poorest case younger  depending on how you look at it  joining me in today's episode is my  fellow countrymen and veteran zelda  theorists dr wily  make sure to head over to his channel  after you're done watching this video  as he has a lot to offer not just on the  subject of zelda but also mario amongst  other topics  now the final two episodes in this  series are going to be a bit different  than the previous ones  unlike zelda link and the other four  champions we don't actually have a path  laid out for any of these characters in  creating a champion  so these journeys will be based on that  which we do know  the most prominent zelda theories as  well as just best guesses in general so  take these paths with a grain of salt  with that out of the way  let's jump right back into it  so since we don't have a definitive path  for the sheikah during the calamity  we first have to establish the starting  point for each character  which we can base on various bits of  information robbie and pura are the  easiest to pinpoint  all research into the guardians and  other ancient sheikah relics  was performed at hyrule castle both the  akala and the clude attack labs were not  established until  after the calamity was over the heart of  controlling the ancient relics and  storing the data collected lies in the  guidance stones  of which a significant amount were also  being kept at the castle  this means that both pura and robbie  were most likely at the castle the  moment the calamity started  they may have even set up a temporary  home in this area  since research was done on a daily basis  and would have saved a lot of time  traveling from kakariko village to the  castle  every day this is further supported by  the following sentence  found in creating a champion on the day  of the great calamity the surviving  sheikah from the castle in hyrule castle  town  fled to their hometown of kakariko  village this indicates that some shika  did indeed live in the main capital of  the hylians  ampura and robbie were most likely among  those who did  impasse a bit trickier though since she  herself was not directly involved in the  research as far as we know  and instead acted as the official  advisor to the royal family  being an advisor doesn't necessarily  mean she would have to be at the castle  at all times  or even live there like the others and  in the new age of calamity gameplay  and trailer we can see that she tagged  along with link and his group for quite  a bit  throughout the events preceding the  calamity on the day of ganon's rise  however  she's not present at the landeru  promenade to meet with zelda  after her pilgrimage to the spring of  wisdom this leaves us with two  options in regards to her most likely  location  either she's at the castle with her  sister and robbie or she is at her  hometown kakariko village  waiting for a party to return from the  promenade now for the sake of pacing  we're just going to pick one of these  locations as a starting point  there's no evidence for or against both  options  and it doesn't really impact the overall  arc of the story too much  so we are going with kakariko village  for this theory  for reasons mentioned earlier as well as  the fact that in age of calamity she's  seen tagging along with  link and zelda at harold castle during  the calamity  sure they could have met up at the  castle but on the other hand  meeting one specific person amidst all  the chaos would undoubtedly be  very difficult so it's safe to assume  that she joined them to the castle from  kakariko  with the position of all characters now  set we can finally start outlining their  paths from the moment the calamity  starts  after zelda and the five champions  witness the rise of ganon  they make their way through to promenade  and towards kakariko  there they rendezvous with impa who tags  along with link and zelda towards hyrule  castle  impa has all the reasons to join them as  she will want to ensure the safety of  her sister pura and other fellow shika  who reside at the castle  they traverse the same path laid out in  the section that covers lincoln zelda  down sahasrara's slope following the  haila river north  across the rabone bridge mabe prairie  and into castle town  through the main gate by the time they  arrive the guardians have been corrupted  and hiro castle itself has turned into  absolute chaos  as mentioned in the story of link and  zelda it's likely that the events at  hyrule castle town will be a playable  section  where the princess hero and empire try  to fight off as many guardians as  possible  they may even make their way up to  hyrule castle itself an age of calamity  does seem to show sections where they  actually are at the castle and not just  a town square  for zelda the main motivation would of  course be to confront ganon himself as  well as find her father king rome who  resides somewhere amidst all the turmoil  going on there  but for impa the main goal would be to  locate her sister pura and her friend  robbie who were likely at the castle  doing their daily dose of research when  disaster struck  this potential playable section up to  hyrule castle might be an actual rescue  mission to attempt to save their loved  ones  impa manages to meet up with pura robbie  and any other surviving shika members  after realizing that hyrule castle and  town are beyond saving and with the area  flooding with more and more guardians  impa urges link and zelda to meet up at  kakariko village and discuss a new  strategy from there  at this point getting as many people to  safety is the main objective  since zelda still hasn't managed to  awaken her power and thus confronting  ganon is futile  with little time to linger impa pura and  robbie gather up as much of the ancient  relics as possible  in an attempt to salvage it for future  use this includes parts of two  guidance stones the very same we find at  the nacluda and akala tech labs in  breath of the wild  from here they would likely make their  escape through the east gate of  castletown  through the romani plains apleian forest  and across the rebony bridge  they then move south along the hylia  river up the sahasrara slope and into  kakariko village though their journey  towards kakariko is a dangerous one  jashika are not the prime target of  ganon's army  that would be link and zelda this would  explain what i managed to reach for  boney bridge ahead of link and zelda  as by the time the hero and princess  reach the bridge it's no longer safe to  cross  and they would have to move south  alongside the other side of the hylian  river  although not being the main target the  sheikah's escape route could still be a  playable section  where impan needs to defend the  scientists and other potential survivors  from any guardians in pursuit of them or  monster hordes obstructing their way  forward as of yet we don't know who the  other playable characters in age of  calamity will be  but since she is accompanied by robbie  and pura one of them might be playable  as well  impasse seems to be the fighter of the  group but there are passages in robbie's  memoirs  that describe him as someone who would  dispose of guardians himself  in a one-on-one situation when he was  younger however  it remains to be seen if either him or  pora will be doing any fighting  since they are scientists first after  all all in all it is safe to say that  the sheikah's escape from hyrule castle  to kakariko was an important one  as the preservation of some of the  ancient technology will prove to be  crucial  in the future now after reaching  kakariko the shika survivors hold up at  the village and nervously await the  arrival of princess zelda  after she fails to show up the worried  impa dispatches various chica warriors  to track her down  creating a champion makes it abundantly  clear that kakariko village was never  touched by the guardians  the natural border of mountains  surrounding the village as well as the  fact that the sheikahs were not ganon's  main focus  kept the village polluted and out of  harm's way but  as we have seen with gerudo town and  recently with goron village in the  latest gameplay demonstrations of age of  calamity  there's always still a possibility of  kakariko village  having to deal with monster attacks this  would grant the option for impa to have  one final gameplay  section where she has to keep her  hometown safe from any potential  invaders  as from this point on her role in the  story as a fighter  would basically end since as far as we  know  impa never left kakariko beyond this  point in the story  in the meantime two of the shika  warriors dispatched by impa locate the  princess and the hero in the fields of  platory plain  in front of fort titano while they carry  the mortally wounded link to the shrine  of resurrection  along with the sheikah side zelda  finally meets up with impa  at the village after discussing a new  strategy zelda continues on her journey  to hyrule's great forest alone to return  the master sword  and face calamity ganon however impa  instructs  robbie and pora to make their way to the  shrine of resurrection  located on the great plateau to assist  in operating the facility  although we don't have any information  on how exactly pura and robbie got from  kakariko to the great plateau the most  likely scenario would be that they  follow the same path as the two shika  warriors carrying link to the facility  with most of the guardians at fort  hatteno disposed of by zelda it is by  far the safest route to take  they move across the road next the  blattery plane and follow the path in  between the duelling peaks  past their village and across the proxim  bridge from there they crossed the  ruined outpost located at the foot of  the plateau and up to the shrine of  resurrection  by this point central hyrule has long  since fallen and the battles here are  over  most of the remaining guardians have  likely moved out of the province in  search for more blood in the surrounding  areas  such as the gerudo province tabantha  region across the bridge of hailia into  the farron region  la and akala this would have granted  link as well as pura and robbie a safer  passage onto the plateau  there might be a small chance that this  journey towards the shrine of  resurrection taken by pura and robbie is  playable  however out of all scenarios presented  this is by far the most unlikely one  we have no idea if either of the two  characters will even be playable first  of all  and second in this point of the story  the main focus would obviously be on  zelda's journey  still we wanted to at least mention the  possibility before finishing up this  episode  as this will be the last gameplay  scenario presented from this moment on  we pretty much know how the story ends  link is laid to rest by pura and robbie  and impa remains in kakariko village  while zelda finally ends the war by  sealing the demon king inside the castle  with ganon now sealed the remaining  guardians and four divine beasts  no longer pose an immediate threat  though the guardians still remain  dangerous if approached they have turned  into mindless drones who roamed the  landscape without coordination or  purpose  after the two shika scientists return to  kakariko village  robbie pura and impa decide to separate  and live their lives in different parts  of hyrule far away from each other  this way they increase the chance that  at least one of them will be alive to  meet with link once he finally wakes up  and assists him on his journey  in the years to come impa becomes chief  of kakariko village while pura and ravi  set up their respective tech labs in the  cluda and akala  pura continues her research into the  ancient chica relics using one of the  guidance stones they managed to salvage  from hyrule castle  and with his modified guidance stone  robbie manages to develop the ancient  arrow the first weapon to be effective  against guardians  some say that this was his way of  atoning for his deepest regret of not  being able to provide  link with the weapons effective against  the guardians on the day of the great  calamity  though his discoveries came decades too  late his inventions will still prove to  be useful when link  finally makes his inevitable return for  the next 100 years since the day of the  great calamity  the three patiently await the return of  the hero  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  [Music]  you

